  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={2n\u2223n\\in N},\\,B={{2}^{n}\u2223n\\in N}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B={2,4,8,16,\u2026}$\n- $A\\cap B=\u2205$\n- $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
  "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\u2205\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={{2}^{n}\u2223n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,16,\u2026}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={2n\u2223n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,\u2026}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cap B & ={2,4,6,8,\u2026}\\text{\u00a0}\\cap {2,4,8,16,\u2026} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,\u2026} \\\\  & \\ne \u2205.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the intersection is not empty, the two sets are not disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
